> Problems I've had thus far are:
> 
> Food Poisoning

Never eat anything dead unless you saw it killed recently. (Except that 
there are of course a couple of corpses that don't spoil, so if you can 
work out which they are you can keep them and eat them later). Old corpses 
will kill you whether or not you are poison resistant.

Most characters start off without poison resistance, so work out which low 
level corpses are poisonous and avoid them. If your pet eats it, it is safe 
for you to eat.

> Gnomish Mines (great place to get some good equipment but usually too
> tough)
There are several ways to handle the gnomish mines. The easiest is to stay 
away until you are tough enough. If you are playing a gnome or dwarf then 
the top levels of the mines are easy. An advanced technique is to make sure 
you handle the top few levels at XL1, but only try this if you know what 
you are doing.

> Wererats (lycanthropy stinks)
Elbereth, ranged weapons, and pets are useful here.

> running out of food

Some characters start with food supplies, others (not all) might find the 
mines a good supply. Sokoban is a pretty good food source also. Failing all 
else, divine intervention. Mostly though, if you killed it, and it isn't 
going to poison you, eat it.

> generally running into monster that kick my butt and ruin all my fun.

Your problem is the word 'into'. Try using 'away from' instead. Use your 
pet more.

